    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><strong>Keoish drover \u2014 four carts of fleeces, bound for the Gradsul autumn market.</strong> Forties. Talks constantly.</p><p>He attached himself to the party on day four because five armed westerners on the Wool Road are free escort, and he has been paying for it in conversation and bad tea ever since. Three drovers work for him and a boy of twelve; one of the drovers is Sev, who has been laughing at Gianni's accent since the day they met.</p><p><strong>Why he exists:</strong> he is the witness. Everything the party does at the Fallow Ford, Vole sees \u2014 and three weeks later Vole is in a market tent in Gradsul telling it to anyone who buys him a drink, which is how the visibility tally becomes the circular's description of them. He is not an informant and not a plant. He is a man who saw something remarkable and cannot stop saying so.</p><p>He knows the road, the tolls, which wool-house will put five people up, and which Gradsul factors are honest \u2014 all of which the party needs, and all of which they will accept without noticing they are buying it with visibility. A real Keoish drover vouching for them on the quay is worth more than any of Caelith's letters, and it is the reason a berth on the <em>Kestrel Wife</em> is available at all.</p>",
        "public": ""
      },
